<title>ITALY: Italy's Venice sees Jan CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Venice sees Jan CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>VENICE, Italy 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Venice said its January consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 2.7 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In December, the Venice inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 3.0 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Venice is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.89 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to December 1996):</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		   0.1   (0.2)	2.7  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Food				0.0   (0.2)	1.3  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	 0.0   (0.0)	3.9  (4.1)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges 0.5   (0.3)	4.2  (4.7)</p>
<p>    Furniture			 0.0   (0.2)	3.6  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Health services		 2.6   (0.0)	2.5  (1.1)</p>
<p>    Transportation		 -0.8   (0.2)	3.1  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture  -0.1   (0.4)     -1.6 (-2.0)</p>
<p>    Education			 0.0   (0.0)	6.1  (5.0)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	0.0  (-0.3)	6.2  (8.4)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services     0.4   (0.1)	0.9  (0.4)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
